From ud34d025a513c07fc at groups.google.com  Mon May 14 21:25:31 2012
From: ud34d025a513c07fc at groups.google.com (Winston Chang)
Date: Mon, 14 May 2012 21:25:31 +0000
Subject: Re: breaks and labels in coord_polar
Message-ID: <N47jbvU2Kaw.OQYjUNHAyD0J@ggplot2-dev.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <N47jbvU2Kaw.WeGgDnq_Ow8J@ggplot2-dev.groups.google.com>
References: <N47jbvU2Kaw.WeGgDnq_Ow8J@ggplot2-dev.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/ggplot2-dev/c/N47jbvU2Kaw/m/OQYjUNHAyD0J>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

I think this is happening because 0 (usually) isn't in the range of the x data, so it's getting dropped from the breaks.

It works if you specify the x limits:

d <- data.frame(x=runif(50, 0, 360), y=runif(50, 1, 10))

ggplot(d, aes(x, y)) + geom_path() +

    scale_x_continuous(limits=c(0, 360), breaks=c(0, 90, 180)) +
    coord_polar()

It may be related to:
https://github.com/hadley/ggplot2/issues/552

-Winston

