Just to clarify: I was not suggesting that themes should implement the
details of such a rel_col() function, but that it might be useful to
define it as a placeholder for future use since it generalises the
current approach (where the user hand-picks various compatible shades
of grey / colours). Its default could be simply,

rel_col <- function(x, ...)  grey(x)

